  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labour law compliance and safety and health at work improved for all workers in line with national laws and international labour standards</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Country Programme Outcome CHN179 aims to promote compliance with working conditions, safety, and health in China and the global supply chain of Chinese enterprises. It has three components:

1. Strengthening OSH Management in SMEs: MSMEs in China often lack effective OSH risk management due to limited awareness, weak policies, and restricted access to OSH services. To address these challenges, the Ministry of Emergency Management (MEM) has implemented the SCORE (Sustaining Competitive and Responsible Enterprises) programme since 2014. The ILO supports MEM in systematically rolling out the SCORE-based OSH programme, helping SMEs improve productivity and working conditions through training and workplace-based interventions. 

2. Building a Modern and Effective Labour Inspection System: The ILO collaborates with the Labour Inspection Bureau of the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security (MOHRSS) to enhance the capacities of labour inspectors. During this biennium, the ILO will support MOHRSS in organizing an international seminar to share global best practices on labour compliance challenges.

3. Promoting Responsible and Sustainable Business Practices: With the global presence of Chinese enterprises, ensuring responsible business conduct (RBC) and labour compliance in international supply chains is crucial. The ILO collaborates with key stakeholders to develop training curricula and guidelines on labour compliance and RBC for Chinese enterprises operating overseas. This includes supporting the China Enterprise Confederation in developing a Guide on labour compliance and RBC, and promoting sustainable practices of Chinese mineral companies in their overseas operations and supply chains in Africa and Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
